---
import BaseLayout from '../components/BaseLayout.astro';
import Circle from '../components/Circle.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="CONTRIBUTE" description="How to suggest a source, report an error, submit a guide, translate, or mirror Original.">
  <header class="page-head">
    <h1 class="page-title"><Circle /> CONTRIBUTE</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Original is a public resource. Corrections, sources, and translations are welcome; the bar is
      evidence, not volume.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>WAYS TO HELP</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Suggest a source:</strong> an official standard, license, public-domain work, or public-interest dataset.</li>
      <li><strong>Report an error:</strong> a broken link, wrong checksum, outdated version, or unclear explanation.</li>
      <li><strong>Submit a guide:</strong> a plain-language explanation that links to primary sources.</li>
      <li><strong>Translate:</strong> a guide or checklist into another language, with the English original linked. See <a href="/guides/translations/">TRANSLATIONS</a>.</li>
      <li><strong>Mirror:</strong> host a copy of the public corpus or a category archive.</li>
      <li><strong>Test:</strong> check the site with a keyboard, screen reader, small screen, or slow connection.</li>
      <li><strong>Get credited:</strong> accepted contributions are listed in the public contributors file.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>WHAT MAKES A GOOD SUGGESTION</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The source is primary, official, or clearly licensed for reuse.</li>
      <li>The URL is stable and the license is stated.</li>
      <li>The content is useful beyond one person or one project.</li>
      <li>You can name the audience and the task it helps with.</li>
      <li>For a correction, include the URL and evidence.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>EDITORIAL RULES</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>No tracking, advertising, affiliate links, or sponsored placement.</li>
      <li>No legal advice; explanations link to the full text.</li>
      <li>Prefer plain language over jargon, and link the jargon when it is necessary.</li>
      <li>Record corrections; do not silently rewrite history.</li>
      <li>Keep third-party texts under their original licenses.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>HOW TO SEND</h2>
    <p>
      Email <a href="mailto:contact@original.wales">contact@original.wales</a> with the subject
      “Original contribution”. For security issues, use
      <a href="mailto:security@original.wales">security@original.wales</a> instead.
    </p>
    <p>
      You can also open an issue on
      <a href="https://github.com/Verlintas/original">github.com/Verlintas/original</a>. Include the
      URL, the problem, and the change you propose. Accepted contributions are credited in
      <a href="https://github.com/Verlintas/original/blob/main/CONTRIBUTORS.md">CONTRIBUTORS.md</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>REVIEW</h2>
    <p>
      Suggestions are reviewed for sourcing, licensing, clarity, and public value. Not every
      submission is accepted; a small, well-sourced library is more useful than a large,
      unmaintained one. Accepted changes are recorded in the
      <a href="/guides/transparency/">corrections log</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
